# Knowledge Sphere Visualization

A 3D knowledge sphere visualization built with [Babylon.js](https://www.babylonjs.com/), featuring a central sphere with a dynamic Node Material effect, origami-inspired node shapes, and interconnected edges representing a knowledge graph. The frontend uses Babylon.js for rendering, with data served by either a Java Spring Boot backend (using `java.io`) or a lightweight Node.js backend powered by [qnode](https://github.com/calbertts/qnode).

## Features
- **3D Visualization**: Central sphere with a glowing Node Material, polyhedral nodes (origami-inspired), and tube edges.
- **Interactivity**: Click nodes to log data; hover for tooltips with labels.
- **Dynamic Materials**: Customizable shaders via the Node Material Editor.
- **Data Integration**: Fetches data from a Java or Node.js (`qnode`) backend.
- **Performance**: Uses instanced meshes for efficient node rendering.

## Tech Stack
- **Frontend**: Babylon.js (v7.34.1), JavaScript, HTML, CSS
- **Backend Options**:
  - Java, Spring Boot (with `java.io` for JSON reading)
  - Node.js with `qnode` (QuickJS-based API)
- **Tools**: Node.js (frontend and optional backend), Maven (Java backend)

## Prerequisites
- [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/) (v16 or higher)
- [Java JDK](https://www.oracle.com/java/technologies/javase-jdk11-downloads.html) (11 or higher, if using Java backend)
- [Maven](https://maven.apache.org/) (if using Java backend)
- A modern web browser (Chrome, Firefox, Edge)

